/target
/mock/target
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
*.rs.bk

# === mockspace-managed — regenerated by `cargo mock`; do not edit by hand ===
# These paths contain AUTO-GENERATED agent integration files. Source templates
# live in `mock/agent/`. Run `cargo mock` to regenerate outputs.
/.claude/
/.github/copilot-instructions.md
/.github/hooks/
/.github/instructions/
/.github/skills/
# === end mockspace-managed ===

# sketch rustc artefacts (research/sketches/ outputs)
mock/research/sketches/*/libsketch.rmeta
mock/research/sketches/*/*.rmeta

# Python bytecode from probe scripts. The panel's probes are python as often
# as rust, and every run leaves a __pycache__ beside the script. One was
# removed by hand in a prior commit, which fixed that instance; this is the
# class.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The marker that keeps a worktree out of the desktop indexer. Every seat gets
# one on creation, and an unmarked build tree costs the indexer a few thousand
# files per run.
.metadata_never_index

# === mockspace-managed build artifacts (do not edit) ===
# Catch-all: every cargo build dir, including nested ones under benches/,
# tests/, and research sketches. A leading-slash /target would miss those.
target/
# === end mockspace-managed build artifacts ===

# Panel probe rustc output dirs. Each `p<N>_run.sh` recreates its own on every
# run, so the binary and the build log are regenerable and the committed `.out`
# beside them is the evidence.
mock/research/*/[0-9]*_probes/p*_out/

# The registry's own rendered pages, one per namespace. They still generate on
# every run and are still there to read; what changed is that they are not
# published, because the shape a table gives them and the content their prose
# columns carry are both written for somebody working on the design rather than
# for somebody using the crates. They come back when there is a form of them
# worth putting in front of a stranger.
#
# Named one by one rather than swept, because `docs/` also holds the design
# documents and those are published.
/docs/DIMENSION.md
/docs/LAW.md
/docs/OBLIGATION.md
/docs/PROBE.md
/docs/PROPOSAL.md
/docs/QUESTION.md
/docs/RETIREMENT.md
/docs/RULING.md
/docs/STRATEGY.md
/docs/TOPIC.md
